- id: '2097744080725774568'
  text: 'Gaussian Splats are quickly becoming one of my favorite ways to move complex
    3D assets between workflows.


    For this test I started with Panthera Spelaea, the Blender 5.2 splash artwork
    by Joanna Kobierska, available from https://t.co/LyZ2iSuWrs under CC-BY.


    Using GPT-6 Astra, I had it build a 200-frame camera rig and send the renders
    directly to @rendernetwork through the API and export a COLMAP data set.


    NEXT: COLMAP → Postshot → Gaussian Splat.


    The result is a real-time, high-fidelity version of an insanely dense asset -
    millions of hairs and all - that I can now bring back into @OTOY Octane, relight,
    reframe, drop into other scenes, or even publish straight to the web.


    Capture the visual complexity once, then carry it anywhere.


    Check out the splat:

    https://t.co/FIFQo7dSI2'
